After our last post about [b]Amoxoques [/b]([url=https://store.steampowered.com/news/app/1411900?emclan=103582791468267608&emgid=3016822062043677866]you can find it here, in case you missed it![/url]) today we're presenting you the remaining ones, ancient creatures designed by our concept team artist, [b]Jorge H Flores[/b]. 

In the world of our [i]Mictlan[/i], the video game, the Amoxoaque represent the spiritual entities who are in charge of safeguarding and protecting the ancient [b]memories[/b] and [b]wisdom [/b]of [b]Teotihuacan [/b](the place where the gods were born) through the transmission of divine teachings and the interpretation of dreams.

[list]
[*] [b]Oxomoco [/b]is the astrologist who is in charge of deciphering the language of the stars; 
[*] [b]Cipactonal [/b]is the one who puts colors to the paintings in order to express the soul of the things that are drawn; 
[*] [b]Tlatetequi [/b]holds (and gives) the gift of words and outlines the magic signs in the codices; 
[*] [b]Xochicauca [/b]gives form to dirt and stones by sculpting sacred images.
[/list]

